This is an early draft for a generic solution for the issues shown in #2798. I still need to add some member functions for things like accessing and resizing.

The central mechanic is probably this cryptic looking method:
```c++
operator T *() &&;
```
The trailing `&&` makes this work only if the object is used as an rvalue. This should make it possible to create a String like this:
```c++
TM::MemBuffer<char> buf { 5 };
// read into the membuffer, at this moment it's still missing an accessor to the memory
TM::String str { std::move(buf), 5 };
```

